            {
                "entry_id": "88c33d3b-9ff9-3de8-b937-048abc3b4c2f",
                "word": "chur",
                "pos": "intj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9b5f176d-0225-38a3-8ef5-8982c9259d14",
                        "entry_id": "88c33d3b-9ff9-3de8-b937-048abc3b4c2f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A strong voicing of agreement, approval, or thanks: awesome!, cheers!, ta!, thanks!."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "New-Zealand",
                            "informal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cfb30761-048e-4084-8ea8-4e8741316964",
                                "sense_id": "9b5f176d-0225-38a3-8ef5-8982c9259d14",
                                "text": "\"Chur,\" Sir Howard [Morrison] hooted. \"Chur doy, chur\", which, translated, means something along the lines of: \"Well done, mate\"."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "180b2e93-2741-4156-a0ac-472f066451fc",
                                "sense_id": "9b5f176d-0225-38a3-8ef5-8982c9259d14",
                                "text": "K[evin] L[ambert]: Got 2 mates; dum as fuk; do nethin 4 me; can drive truks; fly planes, got kidz 2. / T[uhoe] L[ambert]: Cher cuz. Da dumber da better."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1876fca9-8c70-4b14-9655-adcf1ba8c0ad",
                                "sense_id": "9b5f176d-0225-38a3-8ef5-8982c9259d14",
                                "text": "Meanwhile, on the crap-to-chur scale, Tron [i.e., Hamilton, New Zealand] weather is explained without any need for isobars or weather systems – who knew rain and snow down south was so simple?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "55254b3d-b62a-42c4-a059-4a2f6c4493f3",
                                "sense_id": "9b5f176d-0225-38a3-8ef5-8982c9259d14",
                                "text": "Does Mr [Peter] Thiel (chur, bro, by the way!) gain citizenship because the minister judged it “in the public interest because of exceptional circumstances of a humanitarian or other nature relating to the applicant”?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9aa9c7a2-c6e0-4805-bcaa-c5a436038adf",
                                "sense_id": "9b5f176d-0225-38a3-8ef5-8982c9259d14",
                                "text": "[Stan] Walker's closing address is probably closer to the show's reality: \"More whānau … chur!\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "89bf4d51-ea7d-4fd4-bfeb-03c54256ba65",
                                "sense_id": "9b5f176d-0225-38a3-8ef5-8982c9259d14",
                                "text": "If someone’s made me some food, and it tastes really nice, when someone puts it in front of me, I’d say ‘Oh chur’. […] You always say it with a smile on your face. Every time you hear it, it pretty much gives you a smile, so, chur."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "074e6633-b879-3309-99f1-a00991a60ada",
                        "entry_id": "88c33d3b-9ff9-3de8-b937-048abc3b4c2f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A parting salutation: bye, see you later."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "New-Zealand",
                            "informal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "11aa6e19-35db-4a0e-866b-9cddc37a42ee",
                                "sense_id": "074e6633-b879-3309-99f1-a00991a60ada",
                                "text": "Never a dull moment much love to you axe as well. Chur my cuz. [On hearing of the death of Norm Berryman.]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
